}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''King Ingot Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''King Nekokhamen''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is a [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] variant, sharing cost, cooldown and usage in general. Although his stats are lackluster, especially as the game progresses, he can be a great asset for dealing with [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies early on due to the rarity of anti-Floating meatshields. He is generally outclassed by Tank Cat, though, so it should never be used on stages without Floating enemies.

Later in the game, he will need [[Catseye]]s to stay relevant, as Eraser and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall]] can get close to its health, even against Floating. If given the chance to, however, Gold Brick Cat can become a solid alternative to [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]] in stages where spam is important, thus becoming a solid choice for any Floating-heavy stage, particularly when Kotatsu Cat isn't an option, such as in {{4c}} [[Legend Stages]]. Even there, though, it finds competition with [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter]] once the latter becomes available, as Carpenter has significantly higher health against Floating and also targets Red.

==='''True Form'''===
King Nekokhamen is a small improvement, gaining some health and Toxic Immunity for a rare and precious Gold [[Catfruit]]. For this reason, it is not recommended to focus on unlocking him.

With this being said, his health and new ability make him an ideal counter to [[Gobble]] and [[Zollow]], while also bringing him close to Kotatsu's level when it comes to tanking Floating. Unfortunately, his base health remains very low, so he still faces competition from a talented [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]], who costs more but is much more durable despite lacking any abilities.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

