==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 14.2 Update|Version 14.2]], King Nekokhamen's description misspelled "pharaoh" as "pharoah".
*King Ingot Cat being a fusion of several Gold Brick Cats may be a reference to the "[[wikipedia:Rat king|rat king]]" phenomenon.
*King Nekokhamen's Japanese description states that it is a [[wikipedia:World Heritage Site|World Heritage Site]].
*King Nekokhamen's name is a portmanteau of ''neko'', meaning "cat", and [[wikipedia:Tutankhamun|King Tutankhamen]], an ancient Egyptian King.
**This connection is furthered by King Nekokhamen wearing a mask very similar to the [[wikipedia:Mask of Tutankhamun|mask of Tutankhamun]].

